{"id":"word:hebrew:H8064","type":"word","title":"שָׁמַיִם","subtitle":"H8064 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"the sky (as aloft ; the dual perhaps alluding to the visible arch in which the clouds move, as well as to the higher ether where the celestial bodies revolve)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to שָׁמַיִם (H8064) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 421 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"שָׁמַיִם (shâmayim) means the sky (as aloft ; the dual perhaps alluding to the visible arch in which the clouds move, as well as to the higher ether where the celestial bodies revolve) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 16 26."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"שָׁמַיִם","transliteration":"shâmayim","pronunciation":"shaw-mah'-yim","strong":"H8064","lemmaId":"hebrew:H8064","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["הַ/שָּׁמַ֔יִם","הַ/שָּׁמָ֑יִם","הַ/שָּׁמַ֖יִם","הַ/שָּׁמָֽיִם","הַ/שָּׁמַ֨יִם֙"],"morphs":[["HTd/Ncmpa",236],["HNcmpa",90],["HRd/Ncmpa",38],["HR/Ncmpa",16],["HTd/Ncmpa/Sd",11],["HRd/Ncmda",7],["HC/Ncmpc",4],["HC/Ncmpa",4],["HNcmpc",4],["HNcmpc/Sp2ms",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"the sky (as aloft ; the dual perhaps alluding to the visible arch in which the clouds move, as well as to the higher ether where the celestial bodies revolve)","usage":"air, × astrologer, heaven(-s).","full":"H8064. shamayim [ שָׁמַי ] noun masculine Deut 33:28 only plural שָׁמַ֫יִם 421 (Sta §324 a ) heavens, sky (Late Hebrew id. ; Assyrian šamû plural šamê, šamûtu , also šamâmu , compare Phoenician שמם ; Sabean סמה Hom Chr 46, 124 ; Arabic Ethiopic Aramaic שְׁמַיָּא ; Palmyrene, Nabataean שמ(י)ן in proper name (compounded with בעל ) Lzb 153 GACooke 45 ; on plural form see Ba ZMG xiii (1888), 341 f. ); — absolute ׳שׁ Gen 1:1 +, מָ֑יִם - 2:4 +; הַשָּׁמַ֫יְמָה Exod 9:8 +; construct שְׁמֵי Deut 10:14 9 t.; suffix שָׁמֶיךָ Psa 8:4 2 t., שָׁמָיו Deut 33:28 , שְׁמֵיכֶם Lev 26:19 , with verb plural, Hosea 2:23 ; &#8212; 1. a. visible heavens, sky , where stars, etc., are Judg 5:20 ; Gen 15:5 (J), Deut 4:19 ; Gen 1:14-15 , 17 (P), hence הַשּׁ ׳כּוֺכְבֵי 22:17 (JE) = 9 t. (usually as countless), הַשּׁ צְבָא ׳(כָּלֿ) Deut 4:19 ; Jer 8:2 + ( ׳צ 1c ; rarely of angels , ׳צ 1b ; before which fowl fly Gen 1:20 (P), compare Deut 4:17 ; Jer 8:7 ; Prov 30:19 , הַשּׁ ׳עוֺף Gen 2:19 (J), 1:19 (P) + ( עוֺף 1 ), שׁ ׳צִמֹּר Psa 8:9 , שׁ ׳נִשְׁרֵי Lam 4:19 ; as רָקִיע (q. v.) Gen 1:8 (P), Psa 19:2 , with waters beneath and above Gen 1:9 (P, compare 1:7 ), Psa 148:4 , darkened with clouds 1Kin 18:45 , cleared by wind Job 26:13 ; whence comes rain Gen 8:2 (J), Judg 5:4 ; Deut 11:11 +, and dew Gen 27:28 (J), 27:39 (E), Deut 33:28 (poem) +. compare שׁ ׳בִּרְכֹת Gen 49:25 (poem in J), שׁ ׳מֶגֶר Deut 33:13 (poem), but also (destructive) fire 2Kin 1:10 (twice in verse); Job 1:16 + (see also 2a below); ׳הֹבְרֵישׁ Isa 47:13 , i.e. astrologers, compare ׳אוֺתוֺתהַשּׁ Jer 10:2 ; as high Gen 11:4 (J), Amos (:2(opposed to שְׁאוֺל ), 11:6 (opposed to אֶרֶץ ) +, הַשּׁ ׳עַדלֵֿב Deut 4:11 ;as over all the earth, (כָּלֿ)הַשּׁ ׳תַּחַת Gen 6:17 ; 7:19 (both P), Deut 2:25 ; Eccl 1:13 וגו ׳מִתַּחַת (of extermination) Exod 17:14 (E), Deut 7:24 ; 9:14 +; specifically of Israel, שָׁמֶיךָ 28:23 , שְׁמֵיכֶם Lev 26:19 (H); הַשּׁ ׳בֵּין הָאָרֶץ וּבֵין 2Sam 18:9 (hung from tree), 1Chr 21:16 (of angel), compare Ezek 8:3 (Ezekiel in vision), Zech 5:9 (flying ephah); ׳הַשּׁ הַשּׁ ׳מִקְּצֵה וְעַדקְֿצֵה of limits of horizon Deut 4:32 , compare 30:4 ; Neh 1:9 ; Psa 19:7 as made by God Jer 51:15 (opposed to תֵּבֵל ), Psa 8:4 +? Deut 11:21 ; Job 14:12 ; Psa 89:30 ; especially ׳(הַ)שּׁ וְ(הָ)אָרֶץ = universe (compare in Sabean, SabDenkm No.41.42, l.3 ) Deut 3:24 Gen 1:1 (P) + (especially Deuteronomy, Isa 2 , Psalms), + הַיָם Exod 20:11 ; Hag 2:6 , etc., + לָאָרֶץ מִתַּחַת מַיִם Exod 20:4 = Deut 5:8 ,.compare Prov 30:4 , etc.; opposed to תְּהוֺם 8:27 (+ אֶרֶץ 8:29 ) ׳שׁ חֲרָשָׁה וְהָאָרֶץ חֲרָשִׁים as part of future glory Isa 65:17 ; 66:22 . b. phrases are: הַשּׁ ׳אֲרֻבּוֺת (letting rain through) Gen 7:11 ; 8:2 (P), Mal 3:10 (figurative), compare י ׳הֲיַעֲשֶׂה ׳א ׳בַּשּׁ 2Kin 7:2 , 19 , so שׁ ׳דַּלְתֵי Psa 78:23 (for manna), compare שׁ ׳דְָּגַן , 78:24 , שׁ ׳לֶחֶם 105:40 ; הַשּׁ ׳מוֺסְדוֺת 2Sam 22:8 (|| הָאָרֶץ ; in || Psa 18:8 ׳מ חָרִים ), שׁ ׳עַמּוּרֵי Job 26:11 , שׁ ׳חוּג 22:14 ; towards the sky is הַשָּׁמַ֫יְמָה Josh 8:20 (J), Exod 9:8 , 10 (P), Job 2:12 ; Judg 13:20 ; 20:40 ; 2Chr 6:13 ; עַלהַֿשָּׁמַיִם Exod 9:22-23 , 10:21-22 ,(all E), ׳אֶלשֿׁ Deut 32:40 (poem), Dan 12:7 , ׳שׁ alone 1Kin 8:22 , 54 ; Job 35:5 ; Prov 23:5 . 2. a. as abode of God ( ׳י ) 1Kin 8:30 , 32 +? Psa 2:3 ; Isa 66:1 , etc., compare ׳רֹכֵבשׁ Deut 33:26 (poem), Psa 68:34 , whence he rains brimstone Gen 19:24 (J), bread Exod 16:4 (E), compare Neh 9:15 , casts hailstones Josh 11:11 (E), talks with Israel Exod 20:22 (E; Gi 20:19 ) +, compare Gen 21:17 ; 22:11 , 15 (E), looks down Deut 26:15 +, hears his people Psa 20:7 + 10 t. Chronicles, etc.; he thunders ׳בַּשּׁ 1Sam 2:10 ; Psa 18:14 ,|| ׳מִןשֿׁ 2Sam 22:14 ; he bends ( נטה ) ׳שׁ to come down 22:10 = Psa 18:10 , compare 144:5 and ( rend ) Isa 63:19 ; הַשּׁ ׳נִמְּתְּחוּ Ezek 1:1 in vision of God, compare הַשּׁ ׳שַׁעַר Gen 28:17 (E; + אֱלֹהִים בֵּית ); though even הַשּׁ ׳שְׁמֵי the highest heuvens cannot hold him Deut 10:14 ; 1Kin 8:27 ; 2Chr 6:18 , 2:5 ; Neh 9:6 ; Psa 148:4 , שְׁמֵיקֶֿדֶם שְׁמֵי 68:34 ; he is called הַשּׁ ׳אֱלֹהֵי (post-exilic title) Ezra 1:2 2Chr 36:23 ; + 11 t. Ezra Nehemiah; Jonah 1:9 (compare Aramaic, Dan 2:18-19 , 37 , 44 ; in Gen 24:7 add with הָאָרֶץ וֵאלֹהֵי ᵐ5 , as 24:3 ), ׳אֵלהַֿשׁ Psa 136:26 ; his sword is ׳בַּשׁ Isa 34:5 , but also his חֶסֶד Psa 36:6 , צֶדֶק 85:12 , אֱמוּנָח 89:3 , his word fixed 119:89 . &#8212; ׳שׁ are שָׁמָיו (of Israel) Deut 33:28 (poem), שְׁמֵיכֶם Lev 26:19 ; שָׁמֶיךָ Psa 8:4 ; 144:5 , י ׳שְׁמֵי Lam 3:66 , ׳שׁ קָדְשׁוֺ Psa 20:7 . b. Elijah taken up ׳הַשּׁ in whirlwind 2Kin 2:1 , compare 2:11 . 3 ׳הַשּׁ personified in various relations Isa 1:2 ; Jer 2:12 ; Job 15:15 ; Psa 19:2 ; 50:6 = 97:6 ; 89:6 ; 148:4 . 4 ׳הַשּׁ מְלֶכֶת see ׳מ p. 573. I, II. שַׁמָּה see שׁמם . שָׂ֫מָּה see שָׁם . [ שְׁמַ֫יִן ] noun masculine plural heavens (Biblical Hebrew [ שָׁמַי ], שָׁמַיִם , √ שׁמה ); — always emphatic שְׁמַיָּא : 1 visible sky Jer 10:11 ; Dan 4:8 ; 4:10 ; 4:17 ; 4:19 ; 4:20 ; 4:27 ; 4:28 ; שׁ ׳עוֺף 2:38 ; שׁ ׳צִמֲּרֵי 4:9 ; 4:18 ; שׁ ׳טַל 4:12 ; 4:20 ; 4:22 ; 4:30 ; 5:21 ; שׁ ׳רוּחֵי 7:2 winds of the sky ; שׁ ׳עֲנָנֵי 7:13 ; heavens + earth = universe Jer 10:11 , where God shews signs Dan 6:28 . 2 heavens as abode of God Dan 2:28 ; 4:31 , hence, figurative, as ruling 4:23 ( ׳שׁ sometimes = God in Late Hebrew, J, Aramaic, D Worte Jesu 179; Eng.Tr.218 f. ); as abode of angels 4:32 (Dr); elsewhere in phrase שׁ ׳אֱלָהּ 2:18-19 , 37 , 44 ; Ezra 5:11 ; 5:12 ; 6:9 ; 6:10 ; 7:12 ; 7:21 ; 7:23 (twice in verse), שׁ ׳מֶלֶךְ Dan 4:34 , שׁ ׳מָרֵא 5:23 .","rootNote":"dual of an unused singular שָׁמֶה ; from an unused root meaning to be lofty ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 16 26","keyReferences":["1Chr 16 26","1Chr 16 31","1Chr 21 16","1Chr 21 26","1Chr 27 23","1Chr 29 11","1Kgs 8 22","1Kgs 8 23"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":421,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 16 26","book":"1Chr","chapter":16,"verse":26,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"שָׁמַ֥יִם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmpa"},{"reference":"1Chr 16 31","book":"1Chr","chapter":16,"verse":31,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/שָּׁמַ֨יִם֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmpa"},{"reference":"1Chr 21 16","book":"1Chr","chapter":21,"verse":16,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/שָּׁמַ֔יִם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmpa"},{"reference":"1Chr 21 26","book":"1Chr","chapter":21,"verse":26,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/שָּׁמַ֔יִם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmpa"},{"reference":"1Chr 27 23","book":"1Chr","chapter":27,"verse":2